### Manual request collection.
### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or JetBrains HTTP Client.
### Run them top to bottom — later requests reuse tokens captured from earlier ones.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- AUTH ----

# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Demo Person",
  "email": "demo.person@example.com",
  "password": "Str0ngPass!23",
  "role": "ADMIN"
}

### ^ Note: the "role" above is deliberately ignored — the new account is a USER.

@userToken = {{register.response.body.data.accessToken}}
@userRefresh = {{register.response.body.data.refreshToken}}

# @name loginAdmin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "Admin123!pass"
}

@adminToken = {{loginAdmin.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### Current profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Rotate the refresh token (the old one dies immediately)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{userRefresh}}" }

### Change password (revokes every other session)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/auth/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "Str0ngPass!23",
  "newPassword": "An0therPass!45"
}

### Sign out of everything
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout-all
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### --------------------------------------------------------------- POSTS ----

# @name createPost
POST {{baseUrl}}/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "My first post",
  "content": "Written by the authenticated user.",
  "published": true
}

@postId = {{createPost.response.body.data.post.id}}

### Public list (published posts only when anonymous)
GET {{baseUrl}}/posts?page=1&limit=10&sortBy=createdAt&sortOrder=desc

### Search
GET {{baseUrl}}/posts?search=first

### Only my own posts (drafts included)
GET {{baseUrl}}/posts?mine=true
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Read one
GET {{baseUrl}}/posts/{{postId}}

### Update (owner or admin only)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/posts/{{postId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "My first post, revised", "published": false }

### An admin may edit anyone's post
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/posts/{{postId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Edited by an administrator" }

### Delete
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/posts/{{postId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------- DEPARTMENTS ----
### Organisational units. Any signed-in user can read the directory;
### everything that exposes or changes membership is ADMIN only.

### List departments — any signed-in user, includes the member count
GET {{baseUrl}}/departments?page=1&limit=20&sortBy=name&sortOrder=asc
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Search and filter
GET {{baseUrl}}/departments?search=account&isActive=true
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Create one — ADMIN only; the code is stored uppercased
POST {{baseUrl}}/departments
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Information Technology",
  "code": "it",
  "description": "Systems, infrastructure and support."
}

### Read one — any signed-in user
GET {{baseUrl}}/departments/PASTE-A-DEPARTMENT-ID-HERE
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Rename or retire one — ADMIN only
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/departments/PASTE-A-DEPARTMENT-ID-HERE
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Information Technology", "isActive": true }

### The roster — ADMIN only, same filters as GET /users
GET {{baseUrl}}/departments/PASTE-A-DEPARTMENT-ID-HERE/members?page=1&limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Assign users in bulk — ADMIN only
POST {{baseUrl}}/departments/PASTE-A-DEPARTMENT-ID-HERE/members
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userIds": ["PASTE-A-USER-ID-HERE"] }

### Remove one member — ADMIN only; the account is left unplaced
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/departments/PASTE-A-DEPARTMENT-ID-HERE/members/PASTE-A-USER-ID-HERE
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Delete a department — ADMIN only; 409 while it still has members
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/departments/PASTE-A-DEPARTMENT-ID-HERE
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### --------------------------------------------------------------- USERS ----

### Self-service profile update (role/isActive are ignored here)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Renamed Person" }

### List users — ADMIN only, returns 403 for a USER token
GET {{baseUrl}}/users?page=1&limit=20&sortBy=createdAt&sortOrder=desc
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Filter by role and activation
GET {{baseUrl}}/users?role=USER&isActive=true&search=demo
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Filter by department, or find the accounts nobody has placed yet
GET {{baseUrl}}/users?departmentId=PASTE-A-DEPARTMENT-ID-HERE
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/users?unassigned=true
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Create a user with an explicit role — ADMIN only
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Second Admin",
  "email": "second.admin@example.com",
  "password": "Str0ngPass!23",
  "role": "ADMIN",
  "isActive": true,
  "departmentId": "PASTE-A-DEPARTMENT-ID-HERE"
}

### Read one user — ADMIN only
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/PASTE-A-USER-ID-HERE
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Promote / deactivate — ADMIN only (revokes that user's sessions)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/PASTE-A-USER-ID-HERE
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "ADMIN", "isActive": true }

### Move a user between departments — ADMIN only; null clears the placement
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/PASTE-A-USER-ID-HERE
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "departmentId": "PASTE-A-DEPARTMENT-ID-HERE" }

### Delete a user — ADMIN only; their posts cascade
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/users/PASTE-A-USER-ID-HERE
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### -------------------------------------------------------------- BOOKS ----
### The EPUB library: ADMIN uploads, any signed-in user reads.
### Point the file path below at a real .epub on disk.

### List the library — any signed-in user (published books only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?page=1&limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Search the library
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?search=melville&sortBy=title&sortOrder=asc
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Read one book's metadata
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/PASTE-A-BOOK-ID-HERE
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Read the file itself — inline, for an in-browser reader
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/PASTE-A-BOOK-ID-HERE/file
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Download the file as an attachment
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/PASTE-A-BOOK-ID-HERE/file?download=true
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Upload a book — ADMIN only, multipart/form-data
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----Boundary

------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

Moby Dick
------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="author"

Herman Melville
------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="published"

true
------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="moby-dick.epub"
Content-Type: application/epub+zip

< ./moby-dick.epub
------Boundary--

### Edit metadata — ADMIN only (the file itself is immutable)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/books/PASTE-A-BOOK-ID-HERE
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "published": false, "description": "Staged, hidden from readers" }

### Delete a book — ADMIN only; the stored file goes with it
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/books/PASTE-A-BOOK-ID-HERE
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### ------------------------------------------------- EXPECTED REJECTIONS ----

### 401 — no token
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

### 403 — USER reaching for the admin surface
GET {{baseUrl}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 400 — validation failure
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "X", "email": "not-an-email", "password": "weak" }

### 403 — USER trying to upload a book
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----Boundary

------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

Not allowed
------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="moby-dick.epub"
Content-Type: application/epub+zip

< ./moby-dick.epub
------Boundary--

### 400 — a renamed .zip or .pdf is not an EPUB, whatever the extension says
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----Boundary

------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

Impostor
------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="fake.epub"
Content-Type: application/epub+zip

< ./README.md
------Boundary--
